      "writtenOn": "2022-10-04T13:13:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Seth\u0027s brought this up the type change suggestion in a couple of other contexts.\n\nI was wondering why it\u0027s part of DeviceInfo rather than up a level in the CSR payload, SignedDataPayload. With it here, DeviceInfo would be harder to reuse in other, non-CSR protocols that still require device information.",
      "revId": "a4c4a18dc716a9ec4fe6cbcab489a70a2ae0cb0c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "22ff2478_d36fe896",
        "filename": "security/keymint/aidl/android/hardware/security/keymint/DeviceInfo.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 61,
      "author": {
        "id": 1115498
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-04T15:34:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Legacy hold-over from the fact that this was initially a last minute hack to get Widevine CSRs. We can update this, and given the context I think it makes sense, but we need to just message this to the appropriate people and make the associated changes on device and server code.\n\nAlthough for other use cases, I suppose this field could also just be modified to cover them? E.g. \"DevConfig\" \"Provisioning\" etc?",
      "parentUuid": "d6c64c55_a9a6e54a",
      "revId": "a4c4a18dc716a9ec4fe6cbcab489a70a2ae0cb0c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c554bab7_82e63284",
        "filename": "security/keymint/aidl/android/hardware/security/keymint/DeviceInfo.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 61,
      "author": {
        "id": 1139038
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-04T16:35:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If it were repurposed, you\u0027d ideally change the key of the map field to something more generic which is a breaking change again. If we\u0027ve got an opportunity to avoid oddities, it\u0027s worth a shot at least. I\u0027ll send out something with the couple of more invasive changes I\u0027ve been cooking up and we can see where to take if from there.",
      "parentUuid": "22ff2478_d36fe896",
      "revId": "a4c4a18dc716a9ec4fe6cbcab489a70a2ae0cb0c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "78d175ea_b98873b2",
        "filename": "security/keymint/aidl/android/hardware/security/keymint/DeviceInfo.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 61,
      "author": {
        "id": 1833664
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-04T16:41:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"we need to just message this to the appropriate people and make the associated changes on device and server code.\"\n\nDoes this matter to them? It\u0027s an enum on their end either way, and I expect the server to reject any strings it doesn\u0027t recognize. IOW, this feels like purely a \"schema correctness\" change without any practical effect on the consumer of the DeviceInfo.",
      "parentUuid": "22ff2478_d36fe896",
      "revId": "a4c4a18dc716a9ec4fe6cbcab489a70a2ae0cb0c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4bd54d40_4e4af2a5",
        "filename": "security/keymint/aidl/android/hardware/security/keymint/DeviceInfo.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 61,
      "author": {
        "id": 1139038
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-04T16:52:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I took Max to be responding to my question - which I see I missed a question mark - as to why cert_type is a member of DeviceInfo in the first place. I didn\u0027t see any concern with changing the enum to tstr, though correct me if I\u0027m wrong.",
      "parentUuid": "78d175ea_b98873b2",
      "revId": "a4c4a18dc716a9ec4fe6cbcab489a70a2ae0cb0c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "566b6f24_0fe8f1ff",
        "filename": "security/keymint/aidl/android/hardware/security/keymint/DeviceInfo.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 61,
      "author": {
        "id": 1833664
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-04T16:56:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, I think this change is good as-is. Most clients won\u0027t even know/care, but it does mean we can avoid editing the comments just to update the CDDL.\n\nI was mostly wondering who Max had in mind about messaging (someone in APE I suppose?). My POV is they just don\u0027t even care about this change, but if it\u0027s more complicated than that I\u0027d like to understand why.",
      "parentUuid": "4bd54d40_4e4af2a5",
      "revId": "a4c4a18dc716a9ec4fe6cbcab489a70a2ae0cb0c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bf000e1c_2b428786",
        "filename": "security/keymint/aidl/android/hardware/security/keymint/DeviceInfo.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 61,
      "author": {
        "id": 1115498
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-04T19:37:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, the change is totally good as is.\n\nWe need to inform Widevine of this, and figure out what to do about the Widevine HAL which is already adding this in DeviceInfo. And then make the appropriate changes on the server side and alter the API if necessary.",
      "parentUuid": "566b6f24_0fe8f1ff",
      "revId": "a4c4a18dc716a9ec4fe6cbcab489a70a2ae0cb0c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
